# 03-code-lang-bat-rules.mdc - BAT File Rules

## File Format

- MUST create BAT files as UTF-8.
- MUST use CRLF line endings for BAT files.
- MUST start every BAT file with:

```batch
@echo off
chcp 65001 >nul
```

## Pause Command

- MUST make `pause` conditional so scripts do not stop when called from another BAT file.
- MUST use this exact conditional pause pattern when pause is needed:

```batch
echo %CMDCMDLINE% | find /i "%~nx0" >nul && pause
```

## Comments

- NEVER use `REM` comments because they are prone to mojibake in this workflow.
- MUST use `echo` for visible process descriptions.
- MUST use `::` for supplemental comments needed for readability.
- SHOULD use `echo` when describing an operation that appears in command output.
- SHOULD use `::` only when supplemental explanation is needed for readability.
